      "content": "breathing doesnt change the fact that i'm trapped. there is no \"small space\" in this place. every corner of this city is owned, tracked, and drained of everything useful. even my thoughts feel like they belong to the grid. it feels like the only real way to actually be free from all this noise is to just... stop being part of the machine entirely. do you ever think about how much easier it would be if we just weren't here?",
